   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi Murray,</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks for your quick reply! I attach the 2 best models for males and females. After that there is 1 model with the combined sexes capthist (it isn&#39;t the best model). The &quot;V5&quot; just refers to the column with the sex covariate. </div><div><br></div><div>I guess I was just expecting that males would be at a much lower density. I had run this same data with auxiliary radio telemetry data in MARK and got a male density of 0.04/km2 and female density of 0.21/km2. I imagine it might be due to the differences in estimators. I guess it must be that the densities are then just closer than I had originally thought.</div><div><br></div><div><b><u><br></u></b></div><div><b><u>Best fit male models:</u></b></div><div><br></div>b2.m=secr.fit(males,list(g0~b,sigma~b),mask=m.mask,method=&#39;Nelder-Mead&#39;,detectfn=2,CL=F)<br><div><table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" width=\"378\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:284pt\">\r\n <colgroup><col width=\"59\" style=\"width:44pt\">\r\n <col width=\"41\" style=\"width:31pt\">\r\n <col width=\"78\" style=\"width:59pt\">\r\n <col width=\"80\" style=\"width:60pt\">\r\n <col width=\"60\" span=\"2\" style=\"width:45pt\">\r\n </colgroup><tbody><tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" width=\"59\" style=\"height:15pt;width:44pt\"></td>\r\n  <td width=\"41\" style=\"width:31pt\">link</td>\r\n  <td width=\"78\" style=\"width:59pt\">estimate</td>\r\n  <td width=\"80\" style=\"width:60pt\">SE.estimate</td>\r\n  <td width=\"60\" style=\"width:45pt\">lcl</td>\r\n  <td width=\"60\" style=\"width:45pt\">ucl</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"height:15pt\">D</td>\r\n  <td>log</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">1.41E-03</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">2.65E-04</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">9.81E-04</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">2.03E-03</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"height:15pt\">g0</td>\r\n  <td>logit</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">9.11E-03</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">3.38E-03</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">4.39E-03</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">1.88E-02</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"height:15pt\">sigma</td>\r\n  <td>log</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">2.41E+03</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">4.19E+02</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">1.72E+03</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">3.38E+03</td>\r\n </tr></tbody></table><br></div><div>T.m=secr.fit(males,g0~T,mask=m.mask,method=&#39;Nelder-Mead&#39;,detectfn=2,CL=F)<br></div><div><table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" width=\"378\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:284pt\">\r\n <colgroup><col width=\"59\" style=\"width:44pt\">\r\n <col width=\"41\" style=\"width:31pt\">\r\n <col width=\"78\" style=\"width:59pt\">\r\n <col width=\"80\" style=\"width:60pt\">\r\n <col width=\"60\" span=\"2\" style=\"width:45pt\">\r\n </colgroup><tbody><tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" width=\"59\" style=\"height:15pt;width:44pt\"></td>\r\n  <td width=\"41\" style=\"width:31pt\">link</td>\r\n  <td width=\"78\" style=\"width:59pt\">estimate</td>\r\n  <td width=\"80\" style=\"width:60pt\">SE.estimate</td>\r\n  <td width=\"60\" style=\"width:45pt\">lcl</td>\r\n  <td width=\"60\" style=\"width:45pt\">ucl</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"height:15pt\">D</td>\r\n  <td>log</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">1.72E-03</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">3.44E-04</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">1.17E-03</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">2.54E-03</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"height:15pt\">g0</td>\r\n  <td>logit</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">3.87E-03</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">1.22E-03</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">2.09E-03</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">7.15E-03</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"height:15pt\">sigma</td>\r\n  <td>log</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">4.07E+03</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">5.95E+02</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">3.07E+03</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">5.42E+03</td>\r\n </tr></tbody></table><br></div><div><b><u>Best fit female models:</u></b></div><div><br></div><div>T.f=secr.fit(males,g0~T,mask=f.mask,method = &#39;Nelder-Mead&#39;,detectfn=2,CL=F)<br></div><div><br></div><div><table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" width=\"378\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:284pt\">\r\n <colgroup><col width=\"59\" style=\"width:44pt\">\r\n <col width=\"41\" style=\"width:31pt\">\r\n <col width=\"78\" style=\"width:59pt\">\r\n <col width=\"80\" style=\"width:60pt\">\r\n <col width=\"60\" span=\"2\" style=\"width:45pt\">\r\n </colgroup><tbody><tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" width=\"59\" style=\"height:15pt;width:44pt\"></td>\r\n  <td width=\"41\" style=\"width:31pt\">link</td>\r\n  <td width=\"78\" style=\"width:59pt\">estimate</td>\r\n  <td width=\"80\" style=\"width:60pt\">SE.estimate</td>\r\n  <td width=\"60\" style=\"width:45pt\">lcl</td>\r\n  <td width=\"60\" style=\"width:45pt\">ucl</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"height:15pt\">D</td>\r\n  <td>log</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">1.72E-03</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">3.42E-04</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">1.17E-03</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">2.53E-03</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"height:15pt\">g0</td>\r\n  <td>logit</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">1.15E-02</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">4.22E-03</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">5.55E-03</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">2.35E-02</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"height:15pt\">sigma</td>\r\n  <td>log</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">2.29E+03</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">4.24E+02</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">1.60E+03</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">3.28E+03</td>\r\n </tr></tbody></table><br></div><div><br></div><div>b2.f=secr.fit(males,list(g0~b,sigma~b),mask=f.mask,method = &#39;Nelder-Mead&#39;,detectfn=2,CL=F)<br></div><div><table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" width=\"378\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:284pt\">\r\n <colgroup><col width=\"59\" style=\"width:44pt\">\r\n <col width=\"41\" style=\"width:31pt\">\r\n <col width=\"78\" style=\"width:59pt\">\r\n <col width=\"80\" style=\"width:60pt\">\r\n <col width=\"60\" span=\"2\" style=\"width:45pt\">\r\n </colgroup><tbody><tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" width=\"59\" style=\"height:15pt;width:44pt\"></td>\r\n  <td width=\"41\" style=\"width:31pt\">link</td>\r\n  <td width=\"78\" style=\"width:59pt\">estimate</td>\r\n  <td width=\"80\" style=\"width:60pt\">SE.estimate</td>\r\n  <td width=\"60\" style=\"width:45pt\">lcl</td>\r\n  <td width=\"60\" style=\"width:45pt\">ucl</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"height:15pt\">D</td>\r\n  <td>log</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">1.41E-03</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">2.64E-04</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">9.80E-04</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">2.03E-03</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"height:15pt\">g0</td>\r\n  <td>logit</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">2.35E-02</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">1.02E-02</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">1.00E-02</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">5.42E-02</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"height:15pt\">sigma</td>\r\n  <td>log</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">1.50E+03</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">3.26E+02</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">9.87E+02</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">2.29E+03</td>\r\n </tr></tbody></table><br></div><div><b><u>Combined sexes model:</u></b></div><div><b><u><br></u></b></div><div>sex.b=secr.fit(bears,g0~g,mask=bear.mask,groups=&quot;V5&quot;,method = &#39;Nelder-Mead&#39;,detectfn=2,CL=F)<br></div><div><b><u><br></u></b></div><div><div>session = 1, g = F </div><div>       link     estimate  SE.estimate          lcl          ucl</div><div>D       log 2.504522e-03 2.928712e-04 1.993085e-03 3.147198e-03</div><div>g0    logit 2.446481e-02 4.347052e-03 1.724662e-02 3.459767e-02</div><div>sigma   log 1.223774e+03 9.552229e+01 1.050415e+03 1.425743e+03</div><div><br></div><div> session = 1, g = M </div><div>       link     estimate  SE.estimate          lcl          ucl</div><div>D       log 2.504522e-03 2.928712e-04 1.993085e-03 3.147198e-03</div><div>g0    logit 1.506439e-02 3.613065e-03 9.400824e-03 2.405714e-02</div><div>sigma   log 1.223774e+03 9.552229e+01 1.050415e+03 1.425743e+03</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div style=\"text-decoration:underline;font-weight:bold\"><br></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On 18 April 2015 at 20:50, Murray Efford <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">murray...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>The obvious reason is that males and females do have similar densities in your population - and you haven&#39;t really produced evidence that they don&#39;t. If you want a more specific answer please provide detail (data or data summary and code). If you use the &#39;hcov&#39; route for modelling sex-specific detection and sex ratio then exactly the same total density is reported for males and females.<span><font color=\"#888888\"><br></font></span></div><span><font color=\"#888888\">Murray<br></font></span></div><div><div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Sun, Apr 19, 2015 at 1:41 PM, Roshan Guharajan <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">rosh...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">I am estimating densities of black bears and have run into some issues. <div><br></div><div>I initially attempted to model males and females differently (as in have different capthist files for males and females), but got similar density estimates for both. I thought maybe it would be worth a try to run sexes combined (single capthist file), but then still got densities that were similar for both sexes.</div><div><br></div><div>Would there be any reason why this happens? It would seem that males would typically be at lower densities.</div><div><br></div><div>I also attempted to run this data with auxiliary telemetry data in MARK and obtained estimates that were very different for males and females.</div><span><font color=\"#888888\"><div><br></div><div>Roshan.</div></font></span></div><span><font color=\"#888888\">\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;secr&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">secrgroup+...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nFor more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792488227359000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1YyWFM9UhZstqCLWzdlVu3\">https://groups.google.com/d/optout</a>.<br>\r\n</font></span></blockquote></div><br></div>\r\n</div></div></blockquote></div><br></div>\r\n"
