  {
   "id": "ntElY15cRUYJ",
   "from": "Murray Efford",
   "author": "118cea91a1619106",
   "date": "2015-04-19T05:27:28Z",
   "subject": "Re: Male vs Female Densities",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Roshan<br>It won&#39;t help if your &#39;f&#39;emale&#39; models are fitted to male \r\ndata, but I guess you didn&#39;t mean that! Your combined-sex model fits the\r\n same density for both groups - you need<div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">sex</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">.</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">b2 </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> secr</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">.</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">fit</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">bears</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> model </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> list</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">D</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">~</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">g</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> g0</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">~</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">g</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> sigma</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">~</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">g</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">),</span><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">mask </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> bear</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">.</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">mask</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> groups</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot;V5&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> method </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&#39;Nelder-Mead&#39;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> detectfn </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">2</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">CL </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> F</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span></div></div></code></div>(I&#39;ve\r\n taken the liberty of adding sigma~g). You could also try this to get a \r\ndirect estimate of sex ratio (pmix) (see also ?hcov):<br><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">sex</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">.</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">b3 </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> secr</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">.</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">fit</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">bears</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> model </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> list</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">g0</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">~h2, sigma~h2</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"></span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">),</span><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">mask </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> bear</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">.</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">mask</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> hcov</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot;V5&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> method </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&#39;Nelder-Mead&#39;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> detectfn </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">2</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">CL </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> F</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span></div></div></code></div><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\"></span></div></code></div>Murray</div>"
    ],
