     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><br><br><br>On Sunday, April 19, 2015 at 3:14:55 PM UTC+12, Roshan Guharajan wrote:</div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;padding-left:1ex;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-width:1px;border-left-style:solid\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi Murray,</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks for your quick reply! I attach the 2 best models for males and females. After that there is 1 model with the combined sexes capthist (it isn&#39;t the best model). The &quot;V5&quot; just refers to the column with the sex covariate. </div><div><br></div><div>I guess I was just expecting that males would be at a much lower density. I had run this same data with auxiliary radio telemetry data in MARK and got a male density of 0.04/km2 and female density of 0.21/km2. I imagine it might be due to the differences in estimators. I guess it must be that the densities are then just closer than I had originally thought.</div><div><br></div><div><b><u><br></u></b></div><div><b><u>Best fit male models:</u></b></div><div><br></div>b2.m=secr.fit(males,list(g0~b,sigma~b),mask=m.mask,method=&#39;Nelder-Mead&#39;,detectfn=2,CL=F)<br><div><table width=\"378\" style=\"width:284pt;border-collapse:collapse\" border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n <colgroup><col width=\"59\" style=\"width:44pt\">\r\n <col width=\"41\" style=\"width:31pt\">\r\n <col width=\"78\" style=\"width:59pt\">\r\n <col width=\"80\" style=\"width:60pt\">\r\n <col width=\"60\" style=\"width:45pt\" span=\"2\">\r\n </colgroup><tbody><tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15pt\">\r\n  <td width=\"59\" height=\"20\" style=\"width:44pt;height:15pt\"></td>\r\n  <td width=\"41\" style=\"width:31pt\">link</td>\r\n  <td width=\"78\" style=\"width:59pt\">estimate</td>\r\n  <td width=\"80\" style=\"width:60pt\">SE.estimate</td>\r\n  <td width=\"60\" style=\"width:45pt\">lcl</td>\r\n  <td width=\"60\" style=\"width:45pt\">ucl</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"height:15pt\">D</td>\r\n  <td>log</td>\r\n  <td align=